<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:v7">
<!--
    An ARM hard-float function returns a double in d0 and a float in s0
    (option armfloatreturn, default off).

    The default model lists only the 4-byte s-registers, so a double return
    is cut to its low word: fixed() { vmov.f64 d0,#1.5; bx lr } prints
    unsigned int fixed(void) { return 0; }, and a double argument read from
    d0 is never a parameter.

    The raw image below has no ELF container, so it states no calling
    convention: the option leaves it alone, and only an explicit prototype
    brings the double back.

    armfloatreturn_armhf.o (clang -mfloat-abi=hard, source beside it) is a
    relocatable object whose .ARM.attributes says Tag_ABI_VFP_args=1.
    fmtlf_armhf is a linked PIE whose ELF header carries the hard-float flag.
    Pass 1 (option off) reproduces the defect on both; pass 2 (on) returns
    the whole double, takes the d0 parameter, narrows a float converted from
    a double to s0, keeps an integer return in r0 while d0 is also written
    or still holds a callee's double, fills an unused d0 below a used d1 with
    one double, and does not make two floats in s0/s1 one 8-byte parameter.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">080bb7ee1eff2fe1</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="raw_fixed"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option armfloatreturn off</com>
  <com>lo fu raw_fixed</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option armfloatreturn on</com>
  <com>lo fu raw_fixed</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>parse line extern float8 raw_fixed(void);</com>
  <com>lo fu raw_fixed</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/armfloatreturn_armhf.o</com>
  <com>option armfloatreturn off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu scale</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu fixed</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu narrow</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu keep</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu bump</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu second</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu w2</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/fmtlf_armhf</com>
  <com>option armfloatreturn off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu rd</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/armfloatreturn_armhf.o</com>
  <com>option armfloatreturn on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>lo fu scale</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu fixed</com>
